{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a meaningful +4.2% improvement over the RNA-only baseline (config_001, 0.485/0.464), confirming that adding the image modality is beneficial. However, we have zero data on whether multiprofile (capturing multiple spatial profiles per cell) provides additional signal over singleprofile. This is the largest unexplored design axis. config_018 is the minimal logical extension of config_016: it keeps the same model setting (multimodal), RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat), changing only the profile setting to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool). This isolates the effect of multiprofile while minimizing confounding variables (no new encoder, no new fusion method, no complex aggregation). Under a tight budget, resolving whether multiprofile adds value is the highest-information experiment: if it helps, it unlocks a large family of improved configs; if it does not, we can rule out that axis and focus on fusion method or encoder choice next."
}

